# .env.ingest.example — template for running the ingestion pipeline against the
# LIVE site. Copy this to `.env.ingest` (which is gitignored and NEVER committed)
# and fill in your real values:
#
#   cp .env.ingest.example .env.ingest
#
# Then run:  bin/ingest "Danaus plexippus" 5 --prod
#
# Where to find each value:
#   DATABASE_URL          -> Neon dashboard → your project → Connection string
#                            (the same string set as the Fly secret DATABASE_URL)
#   AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID     -> Tigris storage credentials (Fly secret of same name)
#   AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY -> Tigris storage credentials (Fly secret of same name)
#   AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3   -> Tigris endpoint, e.g. https://fly.storage.tigris.dev
#   BUCKET_NAME           -> your Tigris bucket name
#
# Tip: `fly secrets list -a specimen-gallery` shows the NAMES (not values) that
# production uses, so you can confirm you've filled in the right ones.

DATABASE_URL=
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=
BUCKET_NAME=
